Excellent. I have a very clear picture of the design system. Let me capture the key elements:

**Studio design tokens:**
```css
:root {
  color-scheme: dark;
  --bg: #0a0b0e;
  --bg-raised: #0e1014;
  --text: #f1f2f4;
  --muted: #a2a7b3;
  --faint: #71767f;
  --accent: #8b8cf8;
  --accent-strong: #6366f1;
  --green: #4ade80;
  --amber: #f0b34a;
  --line: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.07);
  --line-strong: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.14);
  --surface: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.03);
  --surface-hover: rgba(255, 255, 255, 0.06);
  --font: -apple-system, ...;
  --mono: ui-monospace, ...;
}
```

Motion easings:
```
--ease-apple-spring: cubic-bezier(0.175, 0.885, 0.32, 1.22);
--ease-apple-out: cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1);
--ease-tactile: cubic-bezier(0.2, 0.8, 0.2, 1);
```

Radii: 8, 9, 10, 12, 14, 16, 18, 20, 22, 999px
Type scale: micro-labels 0.62-0.72rem uppercase with 0.06-0.22em tracking; body 0.85-0.92rem; headings 1rem/600 -0.01em; hero clamp(1.55rem, 3.4vw, 2.25rem) 600 -0.03em
Gradients: `radial-gradient(760px 420px at 50% 108%, rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.09), transparent 72%)` and `radial-gradient(900px 520px at 68% -12%, rgba(99, 102, 241, 0.08), transparent 68%)` — the stage background
Avatar gradient: `linear-gradient(140deg, #6366f1, #8b5cf6)`
Primary button gradient: `linear-gradient(135deg, #818cf8 0%, #7c7ff5 100%)`
Shadows: deep soft shadows, `0 40px 120px -20px rgba(0,0,0,0.85)` for wizard panel

Now let me look at the current live site and check the actual live site rendering. Let me also check the current index.html and sync-readme.py, and look at the docs directory on origin/main.

Let me now check the live site and gather remaining key facts. Let me also look at the docs/ folder in origin/main to know what documentation exists (the site should be a "window to the world").

Let me do this in parallel with reading the current index.html.

